  "passage": "In winter, the classroom coat rack was always messy. Jackets fell to the floor, and students often took the wrong ones.\nThe class leader suggested numbering the hooks. Each student got one number for the semester.\nThe problem improved quickly. Jackets stayed in place, and students found them faster.\nHowever, one hook remained empty for weeks because its student was absent with a long illness. A classmate placed a small paper heart on the hook. Soon others added messages.\nWhen the student returned, the hook was full of welcome notes.\nThe coat rack had started as an organization problem. It became a reminder that an empty space can help people remember someone.",
